# PhoenixInspect preview demo session.
#
# Every line below is a command the console host accepts interactively. Nothing here is special-cased for the demo:
# the same commands answer the same way against any dump of any .NET application, within the supported surface.
#
# The incident: an order-fulfillment service stopped dispatching. We have a dump and no logs.

echo == 1. What was this process, and how far did it get? ==

# Ordinary static fields are the part of a service that stays readable without a stack, a thread, or a debugger,
# so they are where an inspection starts. Fully qualified names need no context evidence at all.
eval Contoso.OrderService.Diagnostics.ServiceState.BuildLabel
eval Contoso.OrderService.Diagnostics.ServiceState.ProcessedOrderCount

echo == 2. Did anything fail, and did anyone leave a note? ==

# A Nullable<int> that holds a value and a reference that is genuinely null are different answers, and stay different.
eval Contoso.OrderService.Diagnostics.ServiceState.LastFailureCode
eval Contoso.OrderService.Diagnostics.ServiceState.OperatorNote

echo == 3. Stand where the code stood, and use the names the source uses. ==

# Adopting a frame supplies its namespace, imports, and aliases as name context. Frames are named from snapshot
# metadata, so a script can name the frame it wants instead of guessing a thread ordinal that shifts between runs.
context Program.Main

# Contextual names additionally need import facts from a Portable PDB whose identity matches the module. 'pdb auto'
# probes paths derived from target-side module hints; offering a file proves nothing on its own, and a candidate that
# does not match is rejected.
pdb auto

# Program.cs has 'using Contoso.OrderService.Diagnostics;', so this is the same field as in step 1 — written the way
# the source writes it.
eval ServiceState.BuildLabel
eval ServiceState.LastFailureCode

echo == 4. Follow the state into the object graph. ==

# Adopting the exact object value of a static field is how an inspection reaches an object the handle table alone
# cannot name. From here 'root' is that dispatcher.
root Contoso.OrderService.Diagnostics.ServiceState.Dispatcher
eval root.Region
eval root.QueueDepth

echo == 5. Which batch is stuck, and how badly? ==

eval root.CurrentBatch.BatchId
eval root.CurrentBatch.PendingCount
eval root.CurrentBatch.DestinationHub

# The chain goes as deep as the object graph does. There is no hop limit — only the evidence boundary.
eval root.CurrentBatch.Route.HubCode
eval root.CurrentBatch.Route.Corridor.Name

echo == 6. Why is it stuck? ==

# The failure record is present, so the conditional access reaches it.
eval root.LastFailure?.Code
eval root.LastFailure?.Detail

# The carrier reference is null, so the conditional access short-circuits to null rather than guessing.
eval root.AssignedCarrier?.Name
eval root.AssignedCarrier?.Name ?? "no carrier ever accepted the batch"

# Nobody ever escalated the batch. A conditional hop that meets an exact null short-circuits mid-chain,
# however deep the rest of the chain would have gone.
eval root.CurrentBatch.Escalation?.Review?.Owner ?? "the batch was never escalated"

echo == 7. What happens when the evidence is not there? ==

# A name the type does not declare is a reported stop with a stable diagnostic code, not a fabricated default.
eval root.RetryBudgetRemaining

echo == 8. Constants are evidence too: metadata, not memory. ==

# An enum member or a const is a literal in the module's metadata Constant table, so the snapshot can answer it
# even though no storage slot exists. Pure integer arithmetic folds with checked C# semantics.
eval System.DayOfWeek.Monday
eval Contoso.OrderService.Diagnostics.ServiceState.HandoffWindowSeconds
eval (86400 / 24) / 60

echo == 9. The same object, reached a second way. ==

# The dispatcher is also strongly rooted, so a bounded handle search finds it independently. The traversal counters
# say how exhaustive that search actually was.
objects Contoso.OrderService.Fulfillment.ShipmentDispatcher

echo == 10. Where were the threads? ==

threads 8 6

echo == 11. What was this session allowed to use? ==

status
